IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ada-dates`
IMPORT `ada-core`
IMPORT `ada-seat`

-- Anti-Discrimination Act 1977 (NSW) -- cases for the seat of the person with the complaint (ada-seat.l4). Every
-- expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text (the section is named on each group), never copied from
-- the encoding's output; day counts are shown where they matter (weekdays checked against a calendar: 3 November 2025
-- was a Monday). Edges: 5 and 6 employees; the grounds each exclusion reaches and those it does not; the inherent
-- requirements exception for hiring and dismissal only; under 21 for an offer and for terms; the 12-month day and the
-- day after, from 29 February; the 21 days by hand and by post (the seventh working day, a weekend, a holiday); the
-- 18-month day and the day after; 6 months from 31 August; the 28 days plus 12 months from 1 February 2024; $100,000
-- and $100,001.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases: the person with the complaint`

-- Which single exception fact a case sets (all others false).
DECLARE `Case exception` IS ONE OF
    `X none`, `X statutory`, `X religious`, `X race GOQ`, `X training`, `X ship`, `X special needs`, `X GOQ`,
    `X pregnancy right`, `X super`, `X married couple`, `X public health`, `X drug`, `X inherent`, `X hardship`,
    `X under 21`, `X voluntary scheme`

-- Every input of the exported work question, with the characteristic covered or not, and one exception.
GIVEN g IS A `Ground`, w IS A `Whose characteristic`, `covered` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `less` IS A BOOLEAN, `seg` IS A BOOLEAN, `req` IS A BOOLEAN, `prop` IS A BOOLEAN, `unreas` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `recog` IS A BOOLEAN, `former` IS A BOOLEAN, `formerprop` IS A BOOLEAN,
      s IS A `What the employer did`, `hh` IS A BOOLEAN, n IS A NUMBER, `pe` IS A BOOLEAN, x IS A `Case exception`
GIVETH A `Work answer`
`the work case` g w `covered` `less` `seg` `req` `prop` `unreas` `recog` `former` `formerprop` s `hh` n `pe` x MEANS
    `Was what my employer did unlawful discrimination` g w
        (IF `covered` THEN `total or partial loss of bodily or mental functions or of a part of the body` ELSE `no condition of these kinds`)
        (IF `covered` THEN `my child or step-child, who depends wholly or substantially on me or needs care or support` ELSE `someone else`)
        (IF `covered` THEN `identifies as a member of the opposite sex by living, or seeking to live, as one` ELSE `none of the transgender descriptions`)
        (IF `covered` THEN `is homosexual` ELSE `is neither`)
        `less` (`less`) `seg` `req` `prop` `unreas` `recog` `former` `formerprop` s `hh` n `pe`
        (x EQUALS `X statutory`) (x EQUALS `X religious`) (x EQUALS `X race GOQ`) (x EQUALS `X training`) (x EQUALS `X ship`)
        (x EQUALS `X special needs`) (x EQUALS `X GOQ`) (x EQUALS `X pregnancy right`) (x EQUALS `X super`) (x EQUALS `X married couple`)
        (x EQUALS `X public health`) (x EQUALS `X drug`) (x EQUALS `X inherent`) (x EQUALS `X hardship`) (x EQUALS `X under 21`) (x EQUALS `X voluntary scheme`)

-- Direct discrimination (less favourable treatment on the ground of the person's own characteristic), no exception.
GIVEN g IS A `Ground`, s IS A `What the employer did`, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Work answer`
`direct` g s n MEANS `the work case` g `my own` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE s FALSE n FALSE `X none`

GIVEN x IS A `Case exception`, g IS A `Ground`, s IS A `What the employer did`
GIVETH A `Work answer`
`direct with` x g s MEANS `the work case` g `my own` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE s FALSE 50 FALSE x

`DISMISSED` MEANS `dismissed me`
`REFUSED` MEANS `discriminated in deciding who should be offered employment`
`ARRANGE` MEANS `discriminated in its arrangements for deciding who should be offered employment`
`OFFERTERMS` MEANS `discriminated in the terms on which it offered me employment`
`TERMS` MEANS `discriminated in the terms or conditions of my employment`
`PROMO` MEANS `denied or limited my access to promotion, transfer, training or other benefits of employment`
`DETRIMENT` MEANS `subjected me to some other detriment`

GIVEN s IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Work answer`
`YES` s MEANS `yes: this is unlawful discrimination in work` s
GIVEN s IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Work answer`
`NODEF` s MEANS `no: this is not discrimination as the Act defines it` s
GIVEN s IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Work answer`
`EXCLUDED` s MEANS `no: the section does not apply to this employment` s
GIVEN s IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Work answer`
`EXCEPTED` s MEANS `no: an exception makes it lawful` s

`SMALL` MEANS "(3)(b): the employer employs no more than 5 people (not counting its private household, and counting related bodies corporate)"
`HOUSEHOLD` MEANS ": the employment is for the purposes of a private household"
`PRIVED` MEANS "(3)(c): the employer is a private educational authority"

§§ `Discrimination in work: the section, applicants and employees (ss 8, 25, 38C, 40, 49D, 49V, 49ZH, 49ZYB)`

-- An employee dismissed, or an applicant refused, because of sex by an employer of 20: s 25(2)(c), s 25(1)(b).
#ASSERT `direct` `sex` `DISMISSED` 20 EQUALS `YES` "s 25(2)"
#ASSERT `direct` `sex` `REFUSED` 20 EQUALS `YES` "s 25(1)"
#ASSERT `direct` `sex` `ARRANGE` 20 EQUALS `YES` "s 25(1)"
#ASSERT `direct` `sex` `OFFERTERMS` 20 EQUALS `YES` "s 25(1)"
#ASSERT `direct` `sex` `TERMS` 20 EQUALS `YES` "s 25(2)"
#ASSERT `direct` `sex` `PROMO` 20 EQUALS `YES` "s 25(2)"
#ASSERT `direct` `sex` `DETRIMENT` 20 EQUALS `YES` "s 25(2)"
-- Each ground's section.
#ASSERT `direct` `race` `DISMISSED` 20 EQUALS `YES` "s 8(2)"
#ASSERT `direct` `transgender grounds` `DISMISSED` 20 EQUALS `YES` "s 38C(2)"
#ASSERT `direct` `marital or domestic status` `REFUSED` 20 EQUALS `YES` "s 40(1)"
#ASSERT `direct` `disability` `DISMISSED` 20 EQUALS `YES` "s 49D(2)"
#ASSERT `direct` `responsibilities as a carer` `TERMS` 20 EQUALS `YES` "s 49V(2)"
#ASSERT `direct` `homosexuality` `PROMO` 20 EQUALS `YES` "s 49ZH(2)"
#ASSERT `direct` `age` `REFUSED` 20 EQUALS `YES` "s 49ZYB(1)"

§§ `The exclusions: private household, 5 or fewer employees, private educational authority`

-- s 25(3)(b): "does not exceed 5": 5 is excluded, 6 is not.
#ASSERT `direct` `sex` `DISMISSED` 5 EQUALS `EXCLUDED` (CONCAT "s 25", `SMALL`)
#ASSERT `direct` `sex` `DISMISSED` 6 EQUALS `YES` "s 25(2)"
#ASSERT `direct` `responsibilities as a carer` `DISMISSED` 5 EQUALS `EXCLUDED` (CONCAT "s 49V", `SMALL`)
#ASSERT `direct` `disability` `REFUSED` 1 EQUALS `EXCLUDED` (CONCAT "s 49D", `SMALL`)
-- s 8(3) and s 49ZYB(3) exclude only a private household: a race or age claim against an employer of 2 stands.
#ASSERT `direct` `race` `DISMISSED` 2 EQUALS `YES` "s 8(2)"
#ASSERT `direct` `age` `DISMISSED` 3 EQUALS `YES` "s 49ZYB(2)"
-- Private household, every ground (s 8(3) and s 49ZYB(3) have no paragraphs).
#ASSERT `the work case` `race` `my own` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `DISMISSED` TRUE 50 FALSE `X none` EQUALS `EXCLUDED` (CONCAT "s 8(3)", `HOUSEHOLD`)
#ASSERT `the work case` `age` `my own` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `DISMISSED` TRUE 50 FALSE `X none` EQUALS `EXCLUDED` (CONCAT "s 49ZYB(3)", `HOUSEHOLD`)
#ASSERT `the work case` `disability` `my own` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `DISMISSED` TRUE 50 FALSE `X none` EQUALS `EXCLUDED` (CONCAT "s 49D(3)(a)", `HOUSEHOLD`)
-- Private educational authority: ss 25, 38C, 40, 49D, 49ZH exclude it; ss 8, 49V and 49ZYB do not.
#ASSERT `the work case` `homosexuality` `my own` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `DISMISSED` FALSE 50 TRUE `X none` EQUALS `EXCLUDED` (CONCAT "s 49ZH", `PRIVED`)
#ASSERT `the work case` `transgender grounds` `my own` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `DISMISSED` FALSE 50 TRUE `X none` EQUALS `EXCLUDED` (CONCAT "s 38C", `PRIVED`)
#ASSERT `the work case` `responsibilities as a carer` `my own` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `DISMISSED` FALSE 50 TRUE `X none` EQUALS `YES` "s 49V(2)"
#ASSERT `the work case` `race` `my own` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `DISMISSED` FALSE 50 TRUE `X none` EQUALS `YES` "s 8(2)"
#ASSERT `the work case` `age` `my own` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `DISMISSED` FALSE 50 TRUE `X none` EQUALS `YES` "s 49ZYB(2)"
-- An exclusion is reported before an exception: 3 employees and a genuine occupational qualification.
#ASSERT `the work case` `sex` `my own` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `REFUSED` FALSE 3 FALSE `X GOQ` EQUALS `EXCLUDED` (CONCAT "s 25", `SMALL`)

§§ `The meaning of discrimination (ss 7, 24, 38B, 39, 49B, 49T, 49ZG, 49ZYA)`

-- Not treated less favourably and no unreasonable requirement: no discrimination, whatever the employer's size.
#ASSERT `the work case` `sex` `my own` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `DISMISSED` FALSE 3 FALSE `X none` EQUALS `NODEF` "s 24"
-- s 4 disability: no condition of the listed kinds.
#ASSERT `the work case` `disability` `my own` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `DISMISSED` FALSE 50 FALSE `X none` EQUALS `NODEF` "s 49B"
-- s 49S: caring for someone outside the list.
#ASSERT `the work case` `responsibilities as a carer` `my own` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `DISMISSED` FALSE 50 FALSE `X none` EQUALS `NODEF` "s 49T"
-- s 49T reaches only the person's own responsibilities; s 7 reaches a relative's or associate's race.
#ASSERT `the work case` `responsibilities as a carer` `a relative's or associate's` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `DISMISSED` FALSE 50 FALSE `X none` EQUALS `NODEF` "s 49T"
#ASSERT `the work case` `race` `a relative's or associate's` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `DISMISSED` FALSE 50 FALSE `X none` EQUALS `YES` "s 8(2)"
#ASSERT `the work case` `age` `a relative's or associate's` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `TERMS` FALSE 50 FALSE `X none` EQUALS `YES` "s 49ZYB(2)"
-- s 38A, s 49ZF: neither transgender nor homosexual, nor thought to be.
#ASSERT `the work case` `transgender grounds` `my own` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `DISMISSED` FALSE 50 FALSE `X none` EQUALS `NODEF` "s 38B"
#ASSERT `the work case` `homosexuality` `my own` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `DISMISSED` FALSE 50 FALSE `X none` EQUALS `NODEF` "s 49ZG"
-- Indirect discrimination needs all three: the requirement the person cannot meet, the substantially higher
-- proportion, and unreasonableness (s 24(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `the work case` `sex` `my own` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `TERMS` FALSE 50 FALSE `X none` EQUALS `YES` "s 25(2)"
#ASSERT `the work case` `sex` `my own` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `TERMS` FALSE 50 FALSE `X none` EQUALS `NODEF` "s 24"
#ASSERT `the work case` `sex` `my own` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `TERMS` FALSE 50 FALSE `X none` EQUALS `NODEF` "s 24"
#ASSERT `the work case` `sex` `my own` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `TERMS` FALSE 50 FALSE `X none` EQUALS `NODEF` "s 24"
-- Segregation is discrimination for race only (s 7(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `the work case` `race` `my own` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `DETRIMENT` FALSE 50 FALSE `X none` EQUALS `YES` "s 8(2)"
#ASSERT `the work case` `sex` `my own` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `DETRIMENT` FALSE 50 FALSE `X none` EQUALS `NODEF` "s 24"
-- s 38B(1)(c): a recognised transgender person treated as of the former sex, and the former-sex requirement.
#ASSERT `the work case` `transgender grounds` `my own` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `TERMS` FALSE 50 FALSE `X none` EQUALS `YES` "s 38C(2)"
#ASSERT `the work case` `transgender grounds` `my own` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `TERMS` FALSE 50 FALSE `X none` EQUALS `YES` "s 38C(2)"
#ASSERT `the work case` `transgender grounds` `my own` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `TERMS` FALSE 50 FALSE `X none` EQUALS `NODEF` "s 38B"
#ASSERT `the work case` `sex` `my own` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `TERMS` FALSE 50 FALSE `X none` EQUALS `NODEF` "s 24"

§§ `The exceptions`

-- Race: ss 14, 15, 16, 21; they do not reach sex.
#ASSERT `direct with` `X race GOQ` `race` `REFUSED` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 14 (genuine occupational qualification: race)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X training` `race` `TERMS` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 15 (employment to train in skills to be used outside New South Wales)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X ship` `race` `TERMS` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 16 (employment on a ship or aircraft, engaged outside New South Wales)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X ship` `sex` `TERMS` EQUALS `YES` "s 25(2)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X special needs` `race` `REFUSED` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 21 (special needs programs and activities)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X race GOQ` `sex` `REFUSED` EQUALS `YES` "s 25(1)"
-- Sex: ss 31, 35, 36.
#ASSERT `direct with` `X GOQ` `sex` `REFUSED` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 31 (genuine occupational qualification: sex)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X pregnancy right` `sex` `PROMO` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 35 (rights or privileges in connection with pregnancy, childbirth or breastfeeding)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X super` `sex` `TERMS` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 36 (superannuation)"
-- s 46 for marital or domestic status; for sex a married-couple job is a s 31(2)(i) qualification, asked as such.
#ASSERT `direct with` `X married couple` `marital or domestic status` `REFUSED` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 46 (employment of a married couple)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X married couple` `sex` `REFUSED` EQUALS `YES` "s 25(1)"
-- Superannuation: s 38Q, s 49; no superannuation exception for race, carers or homosexuality.
#ASSERT `direct with` `X super` `transgender grounds` `TERMS` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 38Q (superannuation)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X super` `marital or domestic status` `TERMS` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 49 (superannuation)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X super` `responsibilities as a carer` `TERMS` EQUALS `YES` "s 49V(2)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X super` `race` `TERMS` EQUALS `YES` "s 8(2)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X super` `homosexuality` `TERMS` EQUALS `YES` "s 49ZH(2)"
-- Disability: s 49D(4) reaches refusing the job and dismissal, not terms or other detriment; ss 49P, 49PA, 49Q.
#ASSERT `direct with` `X inherent` `disability` `DISMISSED` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 49D(4) (inherent requirements of the employment, or unjustifiable hardship)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X hardship` `disability` `REFUSED` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 49D(4) (inherent requirements of the employment, or unjustifiable hardship)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X inherent` `disability` `TERMS` EQUALS `YES` "s 49D(2)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X inherent` `disability` `OFFERTERMS` EQUALS `YES` "s 49D(1)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X inherent` `disability` `DETRIMENT` EQUALS `YES` "s 49D(2)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X public health` `disability` `DISMISSED` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 49P (public health)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X drug` `disability` `DISMISSED` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 49PA (persons addicted to prohibited drugs)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X super` `disability` `TERMS` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 49Q (superannuation, insurance)"
-- Carers: s 49V(4), the same two acts.
#ASSERT `direct with` `X hardship` `responsibilities as a carer` `REFUSED` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 49V(4) (inherent requirements of the employment, or unjustifiable hardship)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X inherent` `responsibilities as a carer` `PROMO` EQUALS `YES` "s 49V(2)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X inherent` `age` `DISMISSED` EQUALS `YES` "s 49ZYB(2)"
-- Age: s 49ZYI (under 21: an offer, and terms or conditions, not dismissal), ss 49ZYJ, 49ZYK, 49ZYR, 49ZYS.
#ASSERT `direct with` `X under 21` `age` `OFFERTERMS` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 49ZYI(1) (junior employees: offering employment to a person under 21)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X under 21` `age` `REFUSED` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 49ZYI(1) (junior employees: offering employment to a person under 21)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X under 21` `age` `TERMS` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 49ZYI(2) (junior employees: terms or conditions of an employee under 21)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X under 21` `age` `DISMISSED` EQUALS `YES` "s 49ZYB(2)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X under 21` `age` `PROMO` EQUALS `YES` "s 49ZYB(2)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X GOQ` `age` `REFUSED` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 49ZYJ (genuine occupational qualification: age)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X voluntary scheme` `age` `DETRIMENT` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 49ZYK (voluntary retirement or severance schemes)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X special needs` `age` `REFUSED` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 49ZYR (special needs programs and activities)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X super` `age` `TERMS` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 49ZYS (superannuation)"
-- Part 6: s 54 and s 56 reach every ground.
#ASSERT `direct with` `X statutory` `homosexuality` `DISMISSED` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 54 (acts done under statutory authority)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X religious` `marital or domestic status` `REFUSED` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 56 (religious bodies)"
#ASSERT `direct with` `X religious` `race` `REFUSED` EQUALS `EXCEPTED` "s 56 (religious bodies)"

§§ `Sexual harassment at work (ss 22A, 22B)`

`HARASSED` MEANS `yes: this is unlawful sexual harassment`
`NOT22A` MEANS `no: this is not sexual harassment as s 22A defines it`
`NOT22B` MEANS `s 22B does not reach this: the work relationships it covers do not include this one (Part 2A's other areas, ss 22C-22J, are not encoded here)`

#ASSERT `Was I unlawfully sexually harassed at work` `an unwelcome sexual advance` TRUE `my employer, while I was its employee or was seeking employment with it` EQUALS `HARASSED` "s 22B(1)"
#ASSERT `Was I unlawfully sexually harassed at work` `an unwelcome request for sexual favours` TRUE `a fellow employee, while I was employed by or seeking employment with the same employer` EQUALS `HARASSED` "s 22B(2)"
#ASSERT `Was I unlawfully sexually harassed at work` `other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature` TRUE `a person whose commission agent or contract worker I am or was seeking to become` EQUALS `HARASSED` "s 22B(3)"
#ASSERT `Was I unlawfully sexually harassed at work` `other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature` TRUE `a fellow commission agent or contract worker` EQUALS `HARASSED` "s 22B(4)"
#ASSERT `Was I unlawfully sexually harassed at work` `other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature` TRUE `another partner in a partnership of which I was a partner or was seeking to become one` EQUALS `HARASSED` "s 22B(5)"
#ASSERT `Was I unlawfully sexually harassed at work` `other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature` TRUE `another workplace participant, at a place that is a workplace of both of us, while I was a workplace participant` EQUALS `HARASSED` "s 22B(6)"
#ASSERT `Was I unlawfully sexually harassed at work` `an unwelcome sexual advance` TRUE `a member of Parliament, at a place that is a workplace of both of us, while I was a workplace participant or member` EQUALS `HARASSED` "s 22B(7)"
-- s 22A: the reasonable person test is not met; or there was no unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature.
#ASSERT `Was I unlawfully sexually harassed at work` `an unwelcome sexual advance` FALSE `my employer, while I was its employee or was seeking employment with it` EQUALS `NOT22A`
#ASSERT `Was I unlawfully sexually harassed at work` `no unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature` TRUE `my employer, while I was its employee or was seeking employment with it` EQUALS `NOT22A`
#ASSERT `Was I unlawfully sexually harassed at work` `an unwelcome sexual advance` TRUE `someone else, or somewhere else` EQUALS `NOT22B`
#ASSERT `Was I unlawfully sexually harassed at work` `no unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature` TRUE `someone else, or somewhere else` EQUALS `NOT22A`

§§ `Compulsory retirement (Part 4E: ss 49ZU, 49ZV, 49ZX)`

`RETYES` MEANS `yes: it is unlawful to retire you, require or threaten your retirement, or act to cause it, on the ground of your age (s 49ZV), despite any retirement age in an award or agreement (s 49ZU(2)); a statutory retirement age for a public sector employee has no effect (s 49ZW)`
`RETOFFICE` MEANS `no: Part 4E does not apply to the retirement of the holder of your office (s 49ZX)`
`RETNOTEMP` MEANS `Part 4E does not reach this: it protects employees in New South Wales, including commission agents and contract workers (s 49ZU)`
`RETNOT` MEANS `s 49ZV does not reach this: it makes unlawful only retiring an employee, requiring or threatening retirement, or acting to cause it, on the ground of age`

#ASSERT `Can I be made to retire because of my age` TRUE `none of the excepted offices` `retired me` TRUE EQUALS `RETYES`
#ASSERT `Can I be made to retire because of my age` TRUE `none of the excepted offices` `required me to retire` TRUE EQUALS `RETYES`
#ASSERT `Can I be made to retire because of my age` TRUE `none of the excepted offices` `threatened to retire me` TRUE EQUALS `RETYES`
#ASSERT `Can I be made to retire because of my age` TRUE `none of the excepted offices` `engaged in conduct with a view to causing me to retire` TRUE EQUALS `RETYES`
#ASSERT `Can I be made to retire because of my age` TRUE `a judicial officer` `retired me` TRUE EQUALS `RETOFFICE`
#ASSERT `Can I be made to retire because of my age` TRUE `an officer removable only with the involvement of Parliament and not appointed for a term` `retired me` TRUE EQUALS `RETOFFICE`
#ASSERT `Can I be made to retire because of my age` FALSE `none of the excepted offices` `retired me` TRUE EQUALS `RETNOTEMP`
#ASSERT `Can I be made to retire because of my age` TRUE `none of the excepted offices` `retired me` FALSE EQUALS `RETNOT`
#ASSERT `Can I be made to retire because of my age` TRUE `none of the excepted offices` `none of these retirement acts` TRUE EQUALS `RETNOT`

§§ `Victimisation (s 50)`

`VICYES` MEANS `yes: subjecting you to a detriment on that ground is unlawful victimisation (s 50(1))`
`VIC502` MEANS `no: s 50(1) does not apply to a detriment because of an allegation that was false and not made in good faith (s 50(2))`
`VICNOT` MEANS `s 50 does not reach this: it makes unlawful a detriment imposed on the ground that you did, intended or were suspected of something under the Act`
`ALLEGED` MEANS `I alleged that someone had done something that would contravene the Act`

#ASSERT `Was I unlawfully victimised` TRUE `I brought proceedings under the Act` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `VICYES`
#ASSERT `Was I unlawfully victimised` TRUE `I gave evidence or information in connection with proceedings under the Act` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `VICYES`
#ASSERT `Was I unlawfully victimised` TRUE `they knew I intended to do one of these, or suspected I had done or intended to do one` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `VICYES`
#ASSERT `Was I unlawfully victimised` TRUE `I did something else under or by reference to the Act` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `VICYES`
-- s 50(2) needs both: false, and not in good faith.
#ASSERT `Was I unlawfully victimised` TRUE `ALLEGED` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `VIC502`
#ASSERT `Was I unlawfully victimised` TRUE `ALLEGED` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `VICYES`
#ASSERT `Was I unlawfully victimised` TRUE `ALLEGED` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `VICYES`
-- s 50(2) is about an allegation only: evidence given in bad faith is still protected by s 50(1).
#ASSERT `Was I unlawfully victimised` TRUE `I gave evidence or information in connection with proceedings under the Act` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `VICYES`
#ASSERT `Was I unlawfully victimised` FALSE `I brought proceedings under the Act` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `VICNOT`
#ASSERT `Was I unlawfully victimised` TRUE `I brought proceedings under the Act` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `VICNOT`
#ASSERT `Was I unlawfully victimised` TRUE `nothing under the Act` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `VICNOT`

§§ `Liability of employers and principals (s 53)`

`LIABLE` MEANS `yes: the act is taken to have been done by the employer or principal too, and you may hold both liable, jointly and severally (s 53(1), (2))`
`NOTAUTH` MEANS `no: the employer or principal did not authorise the act, expressly or by implication, before or after it (s 53(1))`
`STEPS` MEANS `no: the employer or principal took all reasonable steps to prevent the contravention (s 53(3))`
`NOT53` MEANS `s 53 does not reach this: it makes an employer or principal answer only for an act its employee or agent did as such that would contravene the Act if the employer had done it`

#ASSERT `Is my employer liable for what its employee did` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `LIABLE`
#ASSERT `Is my employer liable for what its employee did` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOTAUTH`
#ASSERT `Is my employer liable for what its employee did` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `STEPS`
#ASSERT `Is my employer liable for what its employee did` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `NOTAUTH`
#ASSERT `Is my employer liable for what its employee did` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NOT53`
#ASSERT `Is my employer liable for what its employee did` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NOT53`

§§ `Who may complain (ss 87A, 87C)`

#ASSERT `Can this complaint be made` `I do, for myself` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the complaint may be made (s 87A(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can this complaint be made` `I do, for myself and on behalf of others` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the complaint may be made on behalf of others too (s 87A(1)(a)(ii)); the Tribunal decides whether it goes on as a representative complaint (s 101)`
#ASSERT `Can this complaint be made` `a parent or guardian, for a person who lacks the legal capacity to complain` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: a parent or guardian may complain for a person who lacks legal capacity (s 87A(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `Can this complaint be made` `a representative body, on behalf of named people` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the representative body may complain, having satisfied the President of each person's consent and its sufficient interest (s 87A(1)(c), s 87C)`
#ASSERT `Can this complaint be made` `a representative body, on behalf of named people` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: a representative body may complain only after satisfying the President that each person consents and that it has a sufficient interest (s 87C(1))`
#ASSERT `Can this complaint be made` `a representative body, on behalf of named people` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: a representative body may complain only after satisfying the President that each person consents and that it has a sufficient interest (s 87C(1))`
#ASSERT `Can this complaint be made` `an agent, such as a lawyer, for one of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: an agent may make the complaint (s 87A(1)(d))`
#ASSERT `Can this complaint be made` `someone else` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a complaint may be made only by the people s 87A(1) lists`
#ASSERT `Can this complaint be made` `I do, for myself` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a complaint cannot be made about a contravention of a provision for which a specific penalty is imposed (s 87A(1)); that is for a prosecution, and the President may decline such a complaint (s 89B(2)(c))`

§§ `Lodging in time (s 89B(2)(b))`

`INTIME` MEANS `in time: no part of the conduct occurred more than 12 months before the complaint, so s 89B(2)(b) gives no ground to decline it`
`PARTLY` MEANS `partly late: part of the conduct occurred more than 12 months before the complaint, so the President may (but need not) decline the complaint in whole or in part (s 89B(1), (2)(b))`
`LATE` MEANS `late: all of the conduct occurred more than 12 months before the complaint, so the President may (but need not) decline it (s 89B(2)(b))`

-- 12 months after 10 March 2025 is 10 March 2026; after 29 February 2024, 28 February 2025; after 31 August 2025,
-- 31 August 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I lodge my complaint` (`the date` 10 3 2025) EQUALS `the date` 10 3 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I lodge my complaint` (`the date` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `the date` 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `By when must I lodge my complaint` (`the date` 31 8 2025) EQUALS `the date` 31 8 2026
-- Conduct from 10 March 2025 to 1 June 2025.
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`the date` 10 3 2025) (`the date` 1 6 2025) (`the date` 10 3 2026) EQUALS `INTIME`
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`the date` 10 3 2025) (`the date` 1 6 2025) (`the date` 11 3 2026) EQUALS `PARTLY`
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`the date` 10 3 2025) (`the date` 1 6 2025) (`the date` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `PARTLY`
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`the date` 10 3 2025) (`the date` 1 6 2025) (`the date` 2 6 2026) EQUALS `LATE`
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`the date` 10 3 2025) (`the date` 1 6 2025) (`the date` 10 3 2025) EQUALS `INTIME`
-- One act on 29 February 2024: 28 February 2025 is the last day; 1 March 2025 is late.
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`the date` 29 2 2024) (`the date` 29 2 2024) (`the date` 28 2 2025) EQUALS `INTIME`
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`the date` 29 2 2024) (`the date` 29 2 2024) (`the date` 1 3 2025) EQUALS `LATE`

§§ `Requiring referral after a decline (ss 93A, 94B, 96)`

`REFOK` MEANS `in time: the President must refer the complaint to the Tribunal (s 93A(2)); the Tribunal's leave is needed before it can be the subject of proceedings (s 96(1))`
`REFLATE` MEANS `late: the 21 days after the notice declining the complaint have passed (s 93A(1))`

-- Given by hand on Monday 3 November 2025: 21 days after is 24 November 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must I require referral to the Tribunal` FALSE (`the date` 3 11 2025) 0 EQUALS `the date` 24 11 2025
-- Posted Monday 3 November 2025: working days Tue 4 (1), Wed 5, Thu 6, Fri 7, Mon 10, Tue 11, Wed 12 (7); the period
-- runs from and includes 12 November, so its 21st day is 2 December 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must I require referral to the Tribunal` TRUE (`the date` 3 11 2025) 0 EQUALS `the date` 2 12 2025
-- Posted Friday 7 November 2025: Mon 10 (1) ... Fri 14 (5), Mon 17 (6), Tue 18 (7); last day 8 December 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must I require referral to the Tribunal` TRUE (`the date` 7 11 2025) 0 EQUALS `the date` 8 12 2025
-- Posted Saturday 8 November 2025: the same seventh working day, Tue 18 November; last day 8 December 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must I require referral to the Tribunal` TRUE (`the date` 8 11 2025) 0 EQUALS `the date` 8 12 2025
-- Posted Monday 3 November 2025 with one weekday holiday: the seventh working day is Thu 13 November; last day
-- 3 December 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must I require referral to the Tribunal` TRUE (`the date` 3 11 2025) 1 EQUALS `the date` 3 12 2025
#ASSERT `Did I require referral in time` FALSE (`the date` 3 11 2025) 0 (`the date` 24 11 2025) EQUALS `REFOK`
#ASSERT `Did I require referral in time` FALSE (`the date` 3 11 2025) 0 (`the date` 25 11 2025) EQUALS `REFLATE`
#ASSERT `Did I require referral in time` TRUE (`the date` 3 11 2025) 0 (`the date` 2 12 2025) EQUALS `REFOK`
#ASSERT `Did I require referral in time` TRUE (`the date` 3 11 2025) 0 (`the date` 3 12 2025) EQUALS `REFLATE`
#ASSERT `Did I require referral in time` FALSE (`the date` 3 11 2025) 0 (`the date` 3 11 2025) EQUALS `REFOK`

§§ `An unresolved complaint after 18 months (s 93B)`

`UNRES` MEANS `no: a party may request referral only if the complaint has not been declined, terminated or otherwise resolved within 18 months after it was made (s 93B(1))`
`NOTYET` MEANS `not yet: a party may request referral only once 18 months after the complaint was made have passed (s 93B(1))`
`REF3` MEANS `referred: no party objected within 28 days after the President gave notice of the request, so the President is to refer the complaint (s 93B(3))`
`NOREF4` MEANS `not referred: because you objected the President must not refer it, and may terminate it if satisfied there is no reasonable prospect of a conciliated agreement (s 93B(4))`
`REF5` MEANS `referred: the respondent objected, but the President is to refer it unless satisfied there are reasonable prospects of a conciliated agreement (s 93B(5))`
`NOREF5` MEANS `not referred: the respondent objected and the President is satisfied there are reasonable prospects of a conciliated agreement (s 93B(5))`

-- Made 15 January 2025: the 18 months end on 15 July 2026, so a request can be made from 16 July 2026. Made
-- 31 August 2024: the 18 months end on 28 February 2026; requests from 1 March 2026.
#ASSERT `From when can I ask for my unresolved complaint to be referred` (`the date` 15 1 2025) EQUALS `the date` 16 7 2026
#ASSERT `From when can I ask for my unresolved complaint to be referred` (`the date` 31 8 2024) EQUALS `the date` 1 3 2026
#ASSERT `What happens to my request for referral` FALSE (`the date` 15 1 2025) (`the date` 15 7 2026) `I asked` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOTYET`
#ASSERT `What happens to my request for referral` FALSE (`the date` 15 1 2025) (`the date` 16 7 2026) `I asked` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `REF3`
#ASSERT `What happens to my request for referral` TRUE (`the date` 15 1 2025) (`the date` 16 7 2026) `I asked` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `UNRES`
#ASSERT `What happens to my request for referral` FALSE (`the date` 15 1 2025) (`the date` 1 8 2026) `I asked` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `REF5`
#ASSERT `What happens to my request for referral` FALSE (`the date` 15 1 2025) (`the date` 1 8 2026) `I asked` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NOREF5`
#ASSERT `What happens to my request for referral` FALSE (`the date` 15 1 2025) (`the date` 1 8 2026) `the respondent asked` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOREF4`
#ASSERT `What happens to my request for referral` FALSE (`the date` 15 1 2025) (`the date` 1 8 2026) `the respondent asked` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `REF3`
#ASSERT `What happens to my request for referral` FALSE (`the date` 31 8 2024) (`the date` 28 2 2026) `I asked` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOTYET`
#ASSERT `What happens to my request for referral` FALSE (`the date` 31 8 2024) (`the date` 1 3 2026) `I asked` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `REF3`

§§ `Registering a conciliation agreement (s 91A(5)-(9))`

`REGOK` MEANS `you may apply: serve the application and the agreement on each other party (s 91A(7)); if the Tribunal is satisfied a party has not complied, it is to register the provisions it could have ordered, which then take effect as its order (s 91A(8), (9))`

-- 6 months after 31 August 2025 is 28 February 2026; after 15 January 2026, 15 July 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to register my agreement` (`the date` 31 8 2025) EQUALS `the date` 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to register my agreement` (`the date` 15 1 2026) EQUALS `the date` 15 7 2026
#ASSERT `Can I register my agreement` TRUE TRUE (`the date` 31 8 2025) (`the date` 28 2 2026) EQUALS `REGOK`
#ASSERT `Can I register my agreement` TRUE TRUE (`the date` 31 8 2025) (`the date` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `late: the application must be made not later than 6 months after the date of the agreement (s 91A(6))`
#ASSERT `Can I register my agreement` FALSE TRUE (`the date` 31 8 2025) (`the date` 1 9 2025) EQUALS `no: only a written, signed record of an agreement reached after conciliation can be registered (s 91A(5), (6))`
#ASSERT `Can I register my agreement` TRUE FALSE (`the date` 31 8 2025) (`the date` 1 9 2025) EQUALS `no: an application may be made only by a party who is of the opinion that another party has not complied with the agreement (s 91A(6))`

§§ `Reviving an abandoned complaint (s 92C)`

-- Served 1 March 2025: the 28 days end 29 March 2025; 12 months later is 29 March 2026. Served 1 February 2024: the
-- 28 days end 29 February 2024; 12 months later is 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT `By when can I revive my complaint` (`the date` 1 3 2025) EQUALS `the date` 29 3 2026
#ASSERT `By when can I revive my complaint` (`the date` 1 2 2024) EQUALS `the date` 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `Can my complaint be revived` (`the date` 1 3 2025) (`the date` 29 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS `yes: the complaint may be revived (s 92C(2))`
#ASSERT `Can my complaint be revived` (`the date` 1 3 2025) (`the date` 30 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS `late: a complaint taken to be abandoned may be revived only within 12 months after the end of the 28-day period (s 92C(2))`
#ASSERT `Can my complaint be revived` (`the date` 1 3 2025) (`the date` 1 6 2025) FALSE EQUALS `no: the President must be satisfied that you wish to pursue it, that the failure did not happen or ought reasonably to be excused, and that reviving it causes the respondent no undue prejudice (s 92C(2))`

§§ `What the Tribunal may award (ss 108, 111A, 112)`

#ASSERT `The most I can be awarded for my loss` FALSE 40000 EQUALS 40000
#ASSERT `The most I can be awarded for my loss` FALSE 100000 EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT `The most I can be awarded for my loss` FALSE 100001 EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT `The most I can be awarded for my loss` FALSE 250000 EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT `The most I can be awarded for my loss` TRUE 40000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `The most I can be awarded for a failure to comply` TRUE 150000 EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT `The most I can be awarded for a failure to comply` TRUE 99999 EQUALS 99999
#ASSERT `The most I can be awarded for a failure to comply` FALSE 150000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Will the damages be paid to me` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you: damages ordered carry interest from the date the order takes effect (or an earlier date the Tribunal orders) at the District Court judgment rate (s 112)`
#ASSERT `Will the damages be paid to me` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `you, not the representative body that complained for you: the Tribunal may direct how the damages are applied for your benefit (s 108(4), (5)); interest runs as for any damages (s 112)`
#ASSERT `Will the damages be paid to me` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not you: a protected defendant must pay damages for conduct while you were an offender in custody into the Victims Support Fund, which discharges its liability to you (s 111A)`
#ASSERT `Will the damages be paid to me` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not you: a protected defendant must pay damages for conduct while you were an offender in custody into the Victims Support Fund, which discharges its liability to you (s 111A)`
